This example selects the largest measurement and keeps the first one on a tie.

```javascript
const rows = [
  {name: "read", selfMs: 2},
  {name: "sort", selfMs: 9},
  {name: "draw", selfMs: 9}
];
let best = rows[0];
for (const row of rows) {
  if (row.selfMs > best.selfMs) best = row;
}
console.log(best.name);
```

The output is sort. draw ties with sort, so it does not replace it.
